s{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-29T07:57:05Z","updated_at":"2026-04-30T09:13:22Z","body":"@Zireael07 you don't need to step in, I'm having a conversation trying to understand the oddities of the PR, thank you but you're not helping ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4341843899/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"resolved"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5316747779","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119027#issuecomment-5316747779","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119027","id":5316747779,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPOciAw","user":{"login":"widike","id":14108031,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTA4MDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14108031?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/widike","html_url":"https://github.com/widike","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/widike/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/widike/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/widike/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/widike/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/widike/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/widike/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/widike/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/widike/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/widike/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-17T13:32:32Z","updated_at":"2026-08-17T13:32:32Z","body":"The guard fixes `addAt`, but `Bus.move` keeps the same off-by-one, so `AudioServer.move_bus()` still desyncs the JS array after this PR.\n\n`Bus.move` unconditionally does `splice(toIndex - 1, 0, movedBus)`, while `AudioServer::move_bus` inserts at `p_to_pos` when `p_to_pos < p_bus`, at `p_to_pos - 1` when `p_to_pos > p_bus`, and appends when `p_to_pos == -1`. Only the middle case matches.\n\nCompared engine-side ordering (measured, 4.7.1.stable, `AudioServer.move_bus` on a 6-bus layout) against `Bus.move` from `library_godot_audio.js` on master, run verbatim on the same array:\n\n| call | C++ | JS |\n|---|---|---|\n| `move_bus(3, 1)` | `Master, Weapon, Music, SFX, Distant, Radio` | `Weapon, Master, Music, SFX, Distant, Radio` |\n| `move_bus(1, 3)` | `Master, SFX, Music, Weapon, Distant, Radio` | `Master, SFX, Music, Weapon, Distant, Radio` |\n| `move_bus(2, -1)` | `Master, Music, Weapon, Distant, Radio, SFX` | `Master, Music, Weapon, SFX, Distant, Radio` |\n| `move_bus(4, 2)` | `Master, Music, Distant, SFX, Weapon, Radio` | `Master, Distant, Music, SFX, Weapon, Radio` |\n\n`move_bus(3, 1)` displaces Master from index 0, which is the same end state as #119026: Master is the only bus created with `setSend(null)`, so once it is no longer at index 0 the subsequent `set_bus_send` calls reassign its `_send` and Sample playback stops reaching `ctx.destination`.\n\nSuggested, matching the C++ branches:\n\n```js\nstatic move(fromIndex, toIndex) {\n    const movedBus = GodotAudio.Bus.getBusOrNull(fromIndex);\n    if (movedBus == null) {\n        return;\n    }\n    const buses = GodotAudio.buses.filter((_, i) => i !== fromIndex);\n    if (toIndex === -1) {\n        buses.push(movedBus);\n    } else {\n        buses.splice(toIndex < fromIndex ? toIndex : toIndex - 1, 0, movedBus);\n    }\n    GodotAudio.buses = buses;\n}\n```\n\nNote this is an ordering comparison against both implementations, not an audio-output test in a browser. Happy to open it as a separate issue if you would rather keep this PR scoped to `addAt`.\n\nFor anyone hitting the original bug before this lands: declaring the buses in `default_bus_layout.tres` instead of calling `AudioServer.add_bus()` at runtime avoids it entirely, since `set_bus_count` appends and keeps both arrays in the same order.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5316747779/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]